title: AgarwalUncle_Day1
tags: 
position: -94,-392
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic AgarewalUncle>>
<<SetBGSprite GeneralStore>>
<<HideAllCharacters>>

After overhearing his mother discuss struggles of local shopkeepers, Raju visits Agarwal Uncle's general store during busy hours to see if he might need assistance.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

The cramped interior buzzes with activity. Customers squeeze between narrow aisles as the shopkeeper moves constantly between tasks.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
Agarwal Uncle: Arre beta, terrible timing and perfect timing all at once!

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Half my customers want their monthly supplies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Anxious">>
Agarwal Uncle: And the other half need immediate small items.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Tired">>
Agarwal Uncle: But I'm just one person trying to serve everyone at once.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: Uncle ji, you look completely overwhelmed!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: The store is so busy right now. Is there anything I can do to help you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Help? Beta, running a general store isn't like playing shop-shop with your friends.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Real money changes hands here. Customers expect exact change.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
Agarwal Uncle: And one mistake in calculations or inventory can cost me profit.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Anxious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Profit that feeds my family.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Determined>>
Raju: I understand it's serious business, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: But I'm good with numbers and I'm very careful with money.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Maybe I could start with something simple to reduce your workload?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
Agarwal Uncle: Simple? Child, there's nothing simple about retail!

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Every transaction requires checking inventory, calculating totals.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Handling cash, giving correct change.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: And maintaining customer relationships.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
Agarwal Uncle: One dissatisfied customer can damage reputation built over twenty years.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to help, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: You've built such a trusted business that serves our entire neighborhood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Surely there's some way I could assist without causing problems?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Quizzical">>
Agarwal Uncle: You really want to learn about shopkeeping?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Even knowing how demanding customers can be?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
Agarwal Uncle: How precise money handling must be?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Tired">>
Agarwal Uncle: How exhausting these long days become?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I'm not afraid of hard work or demanding customers, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: My father always says that honest business is the backbone of any community.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: And I want to understand what that really means.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: Your father is a wise man, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: But understanding and doing are very different things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Then let me learn by doing, uncle. Give me a chance to prove myself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: Your persistence is admirable, I'll give you that.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Come back another time. We'll talk more when it's not so chaotic.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju exits the crowded store, he carries deep appreciation for retail complexity and strengthened determination to prove his commitment.

<<set $AgarwalUncle_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: AgarwalUncle_Day2
tags: 
position: 423,-115
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic AgarewalUncle>>
<<SetBGSprite GeneralStore>>
<<HideAllCharacters>>

Despite the introduction to demanding retail, Raju returns during restocking, hoping to observe how Agarwal Uncle prepares for business.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

The store emanates methodical efficiency. Agarwal Uncle systematically checks deliveries, updates price lists, and arranges products with precision.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: Back again, beta?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Quizzical">>
Agarwal Uncle: I thought the day's madness might have scared you off.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: Most people don't see the hours of preparation behind every smooth transaction.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Actually, uncle, watching you earlier made me more fascinated, not less.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: I've never seen anyone keep track of so many different items.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: So many prices and customer preferences while maintaining perfect accuracy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Skeptical">>
Agarwal Uncle: Perfect accuracy? Ha! Beta, I make mistakes every day.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Disappointed">>
Agarwal Uncle: Miscounting change, ordering wrong quantities, misreading customer needs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: The difference is I've learned to catch errors quickly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Confident">>
Agarwal Uncle: And fix them before they become bigger problems.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How did you develop such detailed knowledge of inventory?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Curious">>
Raju: And customer patterns? Did you study business?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Or learn through experience?

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Sad">>
Agarwal Uncle: I inherited this store from my father twenty-two years ago.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: When I was barely older than you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Pained">>
Agarwal Uncle: He died suddenly, leaving me with suppliers to pay.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Worried">>
Agarwal Uncle: Customers to serve, and a family to support.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Sad">>
Agarwal Uncle: But no formal business training whatsoever.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: That must have been terrifying, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Neutral">>
Raju: Taking on such huge responsibility so young, with no preparation or guidance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Terrifying, yes. But also necessary.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Proud">>
Agarwal Uncle: This store supported my mother, my younger sister's education.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: And eventually my own wife and children.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Determined">>
Agarwal Uncle: When survival depends on success, you learn faster than any classroom could teach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Astonished">>
Raju: That's incredible, uncle. You built all this expertise through dedication.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Through necessity. No wonder you're so careful about every detail.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Neutral">>
Raju: You understand how much depends on getting things right.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Smiling">>
Agarwal Uncle: You're beginning to understand, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: Retail isn't just about selling products. It's about serving community.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Proud">>
Agarwal Uncle: Building trust. Maintaining relationships that span generations.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Quizzical">>
Agarwal Uncle: You keep expressing interest in helping.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Serious">>
Agarwal Uncle: But retail assistance means different responsibilities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "AgarwalUncle" "Quizzical">>
Agarwal Uncle: What exactly do you think you could contribute to established business operations?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I've been thinking about that, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: And I'm ready to show you rather than just tell you.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As their conversation concludes with Agarwal Uncle's direct inquiry, Raju recognizes his offers have progressed into serious evaluation.

